  "data": {
    "body": "Which of the following statements must be TRUE?\n\n\n(i) The function $T: \\mathbb{R} \\longrightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $T(x)=2 x+1$ is a linear transformation.\n\n(ii) The set of points $\\left[\\begin{array}{l}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right]$ satisfying the equation $x+3 y+2 z=13$ is a subspace of $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$.\n\n(iii) The set $\\left\\{\\left[\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{array}\\right],\\left[\\begin{array}{l}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right],\\left[\\begin{array}{l}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{array}\\right]\\right\\}$ is a basis for $\\mathbb{R}^{3}$.\n\n(iv) The function $T: \\mathbb{R}^{3} \\longrightarrow \\mathbb{R}^{3}$ defined by $T\\left(\\left[\\begin{array}{l}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right]\\right)=\\left[\\begin{array}{c}x+y \\\\ x-y \\\\ z\\end{array}\\right]$ is a linear transformation.",
